. I couldn't size the funding gap beyond Pellham's equity raise.\n\n**Capex plans**\n- Pellham plans 2027 capex up 18%.\n- Norvane Utilities plans it up 12%.\n- Most of it goes to substations and transformers.\n- Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n\n**Debt markets**\n- Debt is open, at a higher cost. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 2026 to 165bp.\n- Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably.\n- Norvane, with the smaller increase, looks able to fund itself through bonds.\n\n**Equity markets**\n- Equity is weak. Two utility share offerings were cut back in size.\n- Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after demand fell short.\n- Pellham hasn't replaced that equity with debt. It is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes \"until financing improves\". I have no leverage or ratings data to show whether it could borrow more.\n\n**Implication:** Expect 2027 capex to come in below the announced plans. That is a negative for grid-equipment demand, which bears on n2's question.\n\n**What would change this view:**\n- A successful or re-priced Pellham follow-on offering.\n- Hybrids or asset sales that cover the gap.\n\nSources: n5.r1 (debt) and n6.r1 (equity).","ttft_ms":1790,"type":"result","duration_ms":42706,"uuid":"5363106e-44f1-44fa-8d24-e89f1bc5f0ea","ttft_stream_ms":1276,"time_to_request_ms":549,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":23,"system_prompt":48,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":36,"input_attachments":114,"input_hooks":15,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":11,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":62,"init_frame_send":14,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":36,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":78,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":16,"message_normalization":30,"client_creation":10,"request_build":50},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":274,"time_to_request_cp